{"id":107291,"title":"Multiresolution Distance Volumes for Progressive Surface Compression","url":"https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=volume data compression rendering","final_url":"https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/m2/1/high_res_d/15005935.pdf","year":null,"kind":"link","source":"os:digital.library.unt.edu","doi":null,"arxiv":null,"sha256":"56a163da695e2b29e6387091c3ad1e419ca5e1599aa27c242acff4078f234f61","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"url","fetched_at":1793234410.1463227,"text_chars":47015,"abstract":"Surfaces generated by scientific simulation and range scanning can reach into the billions of polygons. Such surfaces must be aggressively compressed, but at the same time should provide for level of detail queries. Progressive compression techniques based on subdivision surfaces produce impressive results on range scanned models. However, these methods require the construction of a base mesh which parameterizes the surface to be compressed and encodes the topology of the surface. For complex surfaces with high genus and/or a large number of components, the computation of an appropriate base mesh is difficult and often infeasible. We present a surface compression method that stores surfaces as wavelet-compressed signed-distance volumes. Our method avoids the costly base-mesh construction step and offers several improvements over previous attempts at compressing signed-distance functions, including an {Omicron}(n) distance transform, a new zero set initialization method for triangle meshes, and a specialized thresholding algorithm. We demonstrate the potential of sampled distance volumes for surface compression and progressive reconstruction for complex high genus surfaces.","file":null,"marks":[],"links":["https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/m2/1/high_res_d/15005935.pdf","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=volume data compression rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=volume data compression wavelet","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=vector quantization volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=lossy compression scientific volume data","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=wavelet volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=westermann gross wavelet","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=signed distance field mesh","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=signed box distance function","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=distance map computation volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=octree level of detail rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=implicit surface csg","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=wavelet based multiresolution rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=multi-resolution volume visualization","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=octree volume compression","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=multiresolution decomposed volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=distance field compression","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=domain based octree volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=wavelet volume rendering compression","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=progressive encoding volumetric data","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=octree data structure compression","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=wavelet coefficient quantization error","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=hierarchical wavelet compression","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409821/?q=octree subdivision volume rendering"],"cited_by":[{"path":"11849-distance-based-thresholding.md","name":"Distance-Based Thresholding","k":1},{"path":"11846-zero-set-initialization-of-isosurfaces.md","name":"Zero Set Initialization of Isosurfaces","k":1},{"path":"11848-zero-tree-coding.md","name":"Zero Tree Coding","k":1}]}